.TH MORIARTTY 1 "2026-10-24" "Moriartty 0.9.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moriartty \- private-by-default terminal emulator inspired by PuTTY's pterm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moriartty
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-e\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moriartty
opens a terminal window running your shell. It keeps PuTTY's habits:
selecting text copies it (to the PRIMARY selection), the right mouse button
pastes, and the settings follow PuTTY's configuration tree.
.PP
Ctrl+Right-click inside the terminal opens the menu (Copy, Paste, Find,
New Tab, New Window, Saved Sessions, Settings, Event Log, ...).
.PP
A saved session can run a command instead of the shell, for example
.BR "ssh admin@prod.example.com" .
The drop-down next to the + button, or Ctrl+Shift+S, opens a saved session
in a new window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-load " name"
Use the saved session
.I name
instead of Default Settings, and run its command if it has one.
.TP
.B \-config
Open the settings window first.
.TP
.BI \-title " text\fR, " \-T " text"
Window title.
.TP
.BI \-geometry " columns" x rows
Window size in characters, for example 120x40.
.TP
.BI \-dir " directory\fR, " \-\-working\-directory " directory"
Start in
.IR directory .
.TP
.B \-hold
Keep the window open after the program exits.
.TP
.B \-ls
Run the shell as a login shell.
.TP
.BI \-log " file"
Log all session output to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-e " command " \fR[\fIargs\fR...]
Run
.I command
instead of the shell (or the saved session's command). It is started
directly, not through a shell, and must be the last option.
.TP
.BR \-help ", " \-version
Show usage or the version, and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
The defaults are listed here; every shortcut can be changed or turned off
in Settings, Terminal, Keyboard.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+C ", " Ctrl+Insert
Copy to the clipboard.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+V ", " Shift+Insert
Paste from the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
Find in scrollback.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+= ", " Ctrl+\- ", " Ctrl+0
Zoom in, out, back to normal.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+T ", " Ctrl+Shift+W
New tab, close tab.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+PgUp ", " Ctrl+PgDn ", " Alt+1 ... Alt+9
Switch tabs (with two or more tabs).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+N
New window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Saved sessions menu.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Shift+Up ", " Ctrl+Shift+Down
Jump to the previous or next prompt (with shell integration).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl+click
Open the http(s) link under the pointer.
.SH SECURITY
Pasted text is stripped of escape sequences and other control characters,
and pastes of several lines, or with invisible or direction-changing
characters, ask first. Programs cannot write to the clipboard or read the
window title. Only http and https links can be opened, never automatically.
Settings and log files are created private (mode 0600) and symlinks are
refused. See
.I /usr/share/doc/moriartty/README.md
for the full list.
.SH SHELL INTEGRATION
Sourcing
.I /usr/share/moriartty/shell-integration/moriartty.bash
(or
.IR .zsh ,
.IR .fish )
from the shell's startup file marks prompts and commands with OSC 133
sequences. Moriartty then jumps between prompts, and when a command that ran
for a while ends in a background tab, its name turns bold and the desktop
shows a notice with the tab's number and the exit status.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MORIARTTY_DEBUG
If set, diagnostics are written to standard error.
.TP
.BR TERM_PROGRAM ", " TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION
Set to
.B moriartty
and its version for programs running in the terminal.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where settings are kept (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/moriartty/sessions/
Saved sessions, one TOML file each.
.I Default Settings.toml
applies to every new window.
.TP
.I /usr/share/moriartty/shell-integration/
Shell integration scripts for bash, zsh and fish.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pterm (1),
.BR putty (1)
